        <body>
            <div xml:id="d872">

                <pb facs="1023" n="943" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg943"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. King to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 111.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Is a consular or diplomatic officer who is
                    duly authorized to issue United States passports permitted to issue a passport
                    to a citizen of the United States who is at the time of application residing in
                    the jurisdiction of another official so authorized?</p>
                <p>The statutes and instructions are not clear on this point, but seem to imply that
                    he is not. Will the Department please interpret?</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton King.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
